<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bertrada of Prüm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 721</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Bertrada the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bertrada of Prüm, also called Bertrada the Elder, was a Frankish noblewoman of the early 8th century. In 721 she and her son Charibert founded the abbey of Prüm in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eifel">Eifel</a>, which was refounded and richly endowed in 752 by her granddaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrada-of-laon">Bertrada of Laon</a> and Pippin the Short. Through Bertrada of Laon she was a great-grandmother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bertrada-of-prum.jpg" alt="Bertrada of Prüm" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Hummel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%BCm_40.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
